{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/api/books?bibkeys=OLID:OL7293503M,OLID:OL7293504M,OLID:OL7759896M,OLID:OL8826539M,OLID:OL8939613M,OLID:OL9033120M,OLID:OL9036508M,OLID:OL9248208M,OLID:OL9248209M,OLID:OL9551020M,OLID:OL18673077M,OLID:OL22994526M,OLID:OL27914230M,OLID:OL39808331M&jscmd=details&format=json","file":"data/metadata3000_261025/raw/library-2878bb4a27e889e2.json","retrieved":"2026-10-25T22:22:15.650Z","status":200,"data":{"OLID:OL7293503M":{"bib_key":"OLID:OL7293503M","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7293503M/Just_for_Fun","preview":"borrow","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/justforfun00linu","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7895276-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["HarperBusiness"],"identifiers":{"librarything":["119479"],"goodreads":["2134053"]},"subtitle":"the story of an accidental revolutionary","description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Once upon a time Linus Torvalds was a skinny unknown, just another nerdy Helsinki techie who had been fooling around with computers since childhood. Then he wrote a groundbreaking operating system and distributed it via the Internet -- for free. Today Torvalds is an international folk hero. And his creation LINUX is used by over 12 million people as well as by companies such as IBM.\r\n\r\nNow, in a narrative that zips along with the speed of e-mail, Torvalds gives a history of his renegade software while candidly revealing the quirky mind of a genius. The result is an engrossing portrayal of a man with a revolutionary vision, who challenges our values and may change our world."},"covers":[7895276],"key":"/books/OL7293503M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL2633060A","name":"Linus Torvalds"},{"key":"/authors/OL2633061A","name":"David Diamond - undifferentiated"}],"publish_places":["New York, NY"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"pagination":"xxii, 262 p. ;","source_records":["marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part01.utf8:36763837:873","bwb:9780066620725","marc:harvard_bibliographi